\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Credit horizon}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{credit-assignment}

\p{For an action #{A_t}, the \strong{credit horizon} is the number of later
environment transitions before the feedback used to train that action becomes
measurable. A terminal-only signal on a trajectory of length #{T} gives the
first action horizon #{T}; an immediate process label gives horizon zero.}

\p{This is an FTIP specialization of delayed reward and temporal credit
assignment; Chapter 12 of \citef{sutton2018reinforcement} treats return
prediction across temporal spans.
The definition records delay in environment transitions rather than tokens,
because one agent action may contain many tokens.}

\p{Long horizon does not by itself imply that credit is impossible. It marks
where variance, model assumptions, or additional process evidence enter a
bound.}
